---
epr-meta-version: 1
covers: subtree
purpose: Govern the relocated maintenance LENSES and the memory discipline they serve, near their executable implementations.
rules:
  - id: recall-algorithm-contract
    class: inject
    when: { write: "**/recall*" }
    dedupe-of: .epr-meta/elohim/algorithms/recall-contract.json
    why: >
      Retrieval composition, scope, limits and fitness live in recall-contract.json, and the
      executor that implements them is NATIVE — `epr flow memory recall`, in
      elohim/eprfs/epr-cli/src/flow/memory/recall.rs. Do not re-add a Python recall executor
      here: a second implementation of a pinned algorithm is a second method identity for the
      same receipts. CLI session accounting is enforced locally; shell/MCP bypasses and total
      model tokens remain outside this boundary. A new mechanism must not silently reuse a
      pinned execution session.
    retire-when: >
      No lens under this directory reads or writes recall state. The native execution condition
      was met on 2026-09-10 when the Python recall executor was deleted; this manifest moved here
      with the surviving lenses on 2026-09-11 when `.claude/scripts/memory-kit/` was removed.
---

The algorithm is authored content, not a new protocol-wide EprKind. Its executor refuses
unsupported compositions, bounds discovery/provider/read output and pins contract plus executable
bytes per session. The local session counter is operational accounting, not another work queue.
Dependency seals bind the artifact to its implementation and tests; they do not execute checks.
Run `cargo test --manifest-path elohim/eprfs/Cargo.toml -p elohim-epr-cli --test flow_memory_recall --test flow_concerns_corrections` (the `just gate memory-ceremony` leg).
